# VIRTUAL ALEX VARIANT of the Kit's .gitignore. scripts/build-online-template.mjs copies it into the online template as the tree's .gitignore; the Kit's own .gitignore is not read there.
# The repo is PRIVATE and IS the disk: online there is no machine and no nightly backup, so an ignored memory file is lost every session. vault/, soul.md, soul-core.md, the system/ queues and install state, lane state, outputs/ and .claude/skills/ are therefore TRACKED here.
# What stays out, and why: secrets and credential folders (history is forever, and a private repo is one leaked token from public); derived and regenerable files (search index, locks, generated plists and tokens, backup siblings); raw streams and media (logs, voice and typed transcripts, video, audio); and raw landing zones (inbox/, raw forwarded mail) whose durable form is the vault page a lane writes.
# Kit maintainers: while this file sits under variants/online/ git also reads it as a nested .gitignore for that directory, so a rule here ignores the same path under variants/online/. Nothing there matches today; check with git check-ignore -v before adding a rule that could.

# === SECRETS - never commit; if one is ever staged or pushed, rotate it immediately ===
# A project's keys, tokens and passwords live in its work/NN-*/config/ folder, ignored whole by the
# credential-folder rules further down (work/*/config/ and its name variants).
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.dpapi

# Chrome user-data profile (cookies, session tokens)
**/.browser-profile/

# === dependencies / build artifacts ===
node_modules/
.next/
venv/
.venv/
work/voice/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Lane state is lane memory online, so the Kit's work/*/state/ class deny is gone and what stays out is
# named: the raw forwarded booking emails trip-ops banks whole, and the raw draft text of email-triage.
# The sender tally and the important-thread ledger beside it are memory and are tracked; the
# staged-draft ledger is that raw draft text and is not (so online the sent-vs-draft loop cannot compare
# a draft staged in one session with the mail sent after it). Approved sender rules live in the tracked
# rules.md, because work/*/config/ below is never committed.
work/29-trip-ops/state/
work/07-email-triage/state/staged-drafts.json

# Vault-search FTS5 index: derived from vault/**/*.md, rebuilt on the first search of a session.
scripts/vault-index/

# Recall Spine data: SQLite never enters git (a WAL-mode file without its journal is a torn snapshot) and
# the per-prompt telemetry has no reproducible value. The code under system/recall/ ships.
system/recall/*.db
system/recall/*.db-wal
system/recall/*.db-shm
system/recall/*.jsonl

# === outputs/ is TRACKED online (deliverables live where the disk lives), minus streams and media ===
# outputs/logs/* rather than outputs/logs/: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, and the lane guard's block log is the one log that is evidence rather than a stream.
outputs/logs/*
!outputs/logs/untrusted-lane-blocks.jsonl
outputs/voice/
outputs/typed/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a

# === runtime artifacts / OS noise ===
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
*.log
*.tmp
nul
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Obsidian internals (device-local UI state; online the vault is read on github.com)
.obsidian/
vault/.obsidian/

# Power BI project local cache
**/.pbi/cache.abf
**/.pbi/localSettings.json

# === credential folders and build exports: NEVER, whatever the repo's visibility ===
work/*/config/
work/*/export/
work/*/build/
docs/n8n/*/workflow.json
work/*/configs/
work/*/config-*/
work/*/secrets/

# Classes the Kit's own file keeps out, named by class rather than by one project's path: a dashboard's
# generated data and QA captures, its focus-slot copies of the waiting-on-you queue, a stale metrics dump,
# a spreadsheet builder that hard-codes real figures, workflow backups, Power BI exports, call audio, old
# brand binaries, and raw text dumps at the root. A rule for a path that never exists costs nothing.
work/*/app/public/data/
work/*/qa/shots/
work/*/state/focus.json
work/*/state/last-focus.json
hq-summary.json
work/*/build_workbook.py
scripts/n8n-backups/
work/*/powerbi/*.xlsx
work/*/powerbi/*.csv
work/06-meeting-intel/processed/
brand/archive/
/*.txt

# === system/ is TRACKED online: the queues (human-actions, pending-writes, waiting-on-them), the install
# profile and state, the migrations stamp, travel-state, the run log and the rotate journal are all memory.
# What stays out is named: the credential map (it points at machine locations that do not exist online),
# the quota and cost state (a gate with no online twin), two telemetry logs, and the personal-data
# scanner's allowlist (config for a scanner whose premise, a public repo, does not hold here).
system/credentials-ledger.json
system/quota-state.json
system/cost-tripwires.json
system/vault-reads.jsonl
system/heal-log.jsonl
system/personal-data-allowlist.json

# Backup siblings, anywhere: a copy of a personal file is exactly as personal, and 143 KB of identity
# doubled in history is waste.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.backup
*.backup-*
*.orig
*~
system/*.jsonl.bak
system/*.jsonl.backup*
system/*.jsonl.bak-*

# soul.md is TRACKED online. Its dated copies and variants stay out. The compiled card soul-core.md is the
# one sibling that is memory, and it is re-included AFTER the pattern that swallows it: soul-*.md matches
# soul-core.md, and a re-include only works when it comes later in the file.
soul.md.*
soul-*.md
!soul-core.md
soul.*.md

# Raw-source landing zones: nothing sits in an inbox across sessions online; /ingest moves what is worth
# keeping into vault/sources/, which is tracked.
inbox/*
!inbox/.gitkeep
work/*/inbox/*
!work/*/inbox/README.md

# Per-project raw, cache, processed and output folders: raw landing, cache, call audio with transcripts,
# and a second home for deliverables that outputs/ already is. work/*/data/ is TRACKED online: per-project
# data is the memory class.
work/*/raw/
work/*/cache/
work/*/processed/
work/*/output/

# Generator staging and write locks: never committed anywhere.
.staging/
.staging-backup/
.skills-install.lock/
.alex-lock-*/

# Generated for a machine that does not exist online: launchd plists (from scheduler/schedule.md) and the
# brand tokens CSS (from brand/tokens/tokens.json). Both regenerate in-session when needed.
launchd/
brand/tokens/tokens.css
